# HEDA sample environment file.
# Copy it and fill in what you need: `cp .env.example .env`
# `.env` is gitignored. Every key here is optional; dev and tests run without it.

# Web builds only. Serves the site under a sub-path, e.g. GitHub Pages.
# Read by `vite.config.ts` from `.env` or the shell. Dev servers and builds run
# through the Tauri CLI (`bunx tauri dev` / `bunx tauri build`) use the root and
# ignore it. A bare `bun run build` applies it, so don't package that output
# into the desktop app while it is set.
# BASE_PATH=/heda

# Keys that open legacy v1 `.heda` files so they can be upgraded. Without both,
# v1 files are reported as unsupported. Production web builds (`bun run build`
# outside the Tauri CLI, with TAURI_ENV_PLATFORM unset) replace them with empty
# strings so they stay out of the public site. Dev servers and tests still read
# them from here.
# Ask a maintainer for the values; never commit them.
# VITE_LEGACY_FILE_PASSPHRASE=
# VITE_LEGACY_FILE_SALT=

# Release-only, set as GitHub secrets in CI (`.github/workflows/publish.yml`),
# never needed locally:
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY / TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD (updater signing)
# VITE_LEGACY_FILE_PASSPHRASE / VITE_LEGACY_FILE_SALT (same keys as above)
